# SeedPortraitCert — the emitted certificate data (generated by `gen/emit.py`)

Area `Submission/Work/SeedPortraitCert/`.  All numbers are mantissas at scale `2^40` (as in
the sibling area `SeedCertRay`), the parameter box is `Work.SeedCertRay.Xb` (the certified seed
box of the area `SeedCertNum`).

The ten angle classes are the two `T`-orbits of the period-`5` angles `12/33` and `13/33`:
classes `0 … 4` are `12/33 → 9/33 → 15/33 → 3/33 → 27/33 → 12/33` and classes `5 … 9` are
`13/33 → 7/33 → 19/33 → 28/33 → 10/33 → 13/33`; the successor of class `j` is the class of
`T (θ j)` (`Work.SeedPortraitCert.sucP`).

* `dirBaseP` — the ten base directions `e^{2πi θ_j}`, as mantissa pairs;
* `dskP k` — the descent disks of level `k` (angle-major, `10 × NC` disks);
* `perP` — the *periodic family*: the disks of all levels `k ≥ KT` (one family, one half-plane
  per angle class) — the fixed point of the cyclic pull-back constraints;
* `crtP k`, `crtPerP`, `ifaceCrtP` — the (D1) step certificates `(s, ρ, M)`;
* `dirP k`, `dirPerP`, `ifaceDirP` — the (D2) half-plane directions.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.SeedPortraitCert.Num

